# For the YouTube module's yt-dlp (see 00-run.sh), which runs on the system's
# Python, with what the packaged yt-dlp depends on for speed: pycryptodome
# decrypts the cookies of YouTube's sign-in in a fraction of the time yt-dlp's
# own AES takes on a Pi, requests keeps its connections to YouTube open from
# one request to the next, and brotli shrinks what YouTube sends. ffmpeg puts
# a video's picture and sound back together when the Playlists module
# downloads one for an offline playlist: above 360p YouTube sends them apart.
# os/build.sh skips all of it with OSDOS_YOUTUBE=0.
python3 python3-pycryptodome python3-requests python3-brotli ffmpeg
